`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
Spring Boot 4 split every `spring-boot-starter-*` into an empty POM shell (no class files) plus a real, class-bearing module with the same name minus "starter" — confirmed by three sibling `index.json` files in this repo (`spring-boot-starter-couchbase`, `spring-boot-starter-couchbase-test`, `spring-boot-starter-data-couchbase`) that all say "contains only META-INF, use `spring-boot-<x>:4.1.1` instead." The issue's artifact, `spring-boot-data-couchbase-test` (no "starter"), is exactly that real module — it's the one carrying the `@DataCouchbaseTest` test-slice annotation and its auto-configuration classes.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

Key findings from the worktree (no network access was available, so this is based on repo precedent + domain knowledge of Spring Boot's Couchbase test-slice design):

- **No Couchbase Docker infrastructure exists yet** in `tests/tck-build-logic/.../allowed-docker-images/` (only sftp, mosquitto, greenmail, mariadb, microcks, mssql, mysql, nats, nginx, opengauss, postgres, rabbitmq, ryuk are pinned).
- **Couchbase has no embedded/in-memory mode** (unlike `@DataJpaTest`'s default H2). Spring Boot's `CouchbaseAutoConfiguration`/`CouchbaseDataAutoConfiguration` eagerly open a real `Cluster`/`Bucket`, so a `@DataCouchbaseTest`-based context only loads successfully against a live server.
- **This repo's own precedent confirms the pattern**: `tests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-testcontainers/4.1.1/build.gradle` adds an extra testcontainers module (`com.redis:testcontainers-redis:2.2.4`) beyond the scaffold defaults specifically to exercise a `@ServiceConnection`-backed container. The idiomatic, documented way to exercise `@DataCouchbaseTest` is the analogous `@Container CouchbaseContainer` + `@ServiceConnection` pattern, requiring the `org.testcontainers:couchbase` module and a `couchbase/server` image — neither of which the generated scaffold provides (it only adds the library jar + assertj-core).

Since this satisfies "concrete evidence that extra setup is needed," my decision is `advisory_preparation`.

